<title>AUSTRIA: Austria rejects Creditanstalt bid.</title>
<headline>Austria rejects Creditanstalt bid.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>EA Generali, head of the Austro-Italian-German group bidding for the government's stake in Creditanstalt-Bankverein, on Monday said Finance Minister Viktor Klima had turned down the group's offer.</p>
<p>&quot;The consortium regrets that it was not able to fully meet the expectations of the Finance Ministry,&quot; EA Generali said in a press statement. &quot;It can therefore be expected, that a new round of bidding will follow.&quot;  </p>
<p>EA Generali said the main reason for the failed bid was that the consortium, which also includes Germany's Commerzbank and Banca Commerciale Italiana, did not present a bid to take over the government's entire 70 percent voting stake.</p>
<p>EA Generali said the consortium remains interested in Austria's flagship bank and cited &quot;a particular wish to include savings bank Die Erste in mutual considerations over the privatisation of CA.&quot;</p>
</text>
